      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>All For Logan is a community-based nonprofit organization dedicated to promoting cultural preservation, economic development, and community wellness in the historic neighborhood of Barrio Logan. Our mission is to uplift the voices of residents, support local artists and small businesses, and foster inclusive public spaces through cultural programming, and direct community engagement. We accomplish this by organizing free community events, supporting arts and education initiatives, and empower our underserved communities. Our purpose is to ensure that Barrio Logan remains a vibrant, thriving, and resilient community for generations to come.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Cultural Events &amp; Public Programming: We organized and produced several free, family-friendly events, including the annual Día de Muertos Celebration in Barrio Logan, Small Business Saturday, Barrio Art Crawl, Funded a community gallery space that showcases monthly artists and acts as a community gathering space for resources, The Rolodex project- A digital database of local artists, the Dia De Muertos Artist Residency program. Along with our community partners we co-organized Barrio Art Crawl, Sonidos Del Barrio mini concert series, Barrio Logan Snow Day, The Barrio Logan Science and Art Expo, and Chicano Park Day. These free community events attracted thousands of attendees and featured local artists, live performances, free workshops, and wellness activities that celebrated the heritage and diversity of the neighborhood.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>77529</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Economic Support for Small Businesses: We partnered with local entrepreneurs and hospitality providers to launch campaigns that highlight and promote small, independently owned businesses in Barrio Logan. These efforts have helped drive foot traffic, increase visibility, and sustain local commerce.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>1738</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Beautification &amp; Maintenance: During our public events, we employed local contractors and vendors to provide cleanup and logistical support, ensuring that community spaces remain safe, accessible, and welcoming for all.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>2600</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
